{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791051540,"nonce":"ikhNiF0oUZ1Kfll7whRN9fIKTIw=","title":"Host modules: object and string results are never released","message":"A ZynML program calling host members through add_host_modules leaks: an object a host member returns is a foreign box the program owns, and nothing calls zyntax_box_free on it (which would release the host word) unless drop glue covers extern types; a string result is read out of its box (zyntax_box_get_opaque) and the box, which owns the string, is kept. Argument boxes and scalar result boxes are freed by the generated members. A loop creating host objects grows the host's live set and the heap without bound. Needs drop glue for extern-typed locals (release at scope exit) and a string read that copies out and frees the box.","files":null}]}